  "obligation": "Resolve legacy delegate labels into shared residual handlers and lexical exceptional continuations, preserving identity, payload, tail-frame lifetime and exact skipped-handler scope.",
  "representation": "Each lexical destination owns a temporary Delegation record with one exception frame slot and forward jump sites. Delegated protected regions write the original exception directly to that slot. Existing handler and jump operations route to a LoadLocal/WasmThrowRef continuation at the destination boundary. Normal completion bypasses it; nested outgoing delegation includes incoming continuations in its region. Boundaries resolve and discard fixups; caught-arm boundaries propagate outside that catch, body boundaries retain the target handler and function boundaries propagate to the caller. PC-bounded handlers cease to apply after branches and tail frame replacement. All destinations use existing checked local allocation, jump patching and protected-region construction. No runtime handler metadata, cell, opcode, residual format or executor is added.",
  "scope": "Fourteen matching pinned files in disjoint exception and structured-control groups, thirteen focused directives and fourteen Node observations. Only affected runtime/frontend checks and all-target profile checks ran; no full suites, expectations, skips or inventory changes.",
